issue_comments.body:
Add `protect` and `release` methods to keep the consistency of last_host_node.
```
    def _protect_prefetch_anchor(self, node: TreeNode) -> None:
        node.protect_host()
        if self.host_memory_mode == "buffer_only":
            self.inc_lock_ref(node)

    def _release_prefetch_anchor(self, node: TreeNode) -> None:
        if self.host_memory_mode == "buffer_only":
            self.dec_lock_ref(node)
        node.release_host()
```
I wrote a demo to verify the correctness. REF: https://github.com/kvcache-ai/sglang/tree/copilot/pr20535-hicache-tests

Checked whether the `_protect_prefetch_anchor`/`_release_prefetch_anchor` fix from the demo branch (kvcache-ai/sglang@copilot/pr20535-hicache-tests) made it into this PR — it hasn't. The current diff to `hiradix_cache.py` doesn't have either method; the lock_ref pinning for the prefetch anchor in `buffer_only` mode that @stmatengss demonstrated back in April is still not present here.

So as it stands, the concern from April 20 (`last_host_node` protected on the host side but not pinned via `lock_ref`, leaving the prefetch anchor evictable mid-prefetch in `buffer_only` mode) looks like it's still open in the current head (`3e67acc5`), separately from the merge conflicts blocking the merge itself.

@vladnosiv, given how much churn there's been in hicache since April, might be worth pulling the two methods from the demo branch directly into your rebase rather than re-deriving them, since @stmatengss already validated that specific fix works. Would also close out the one piece of review feedback that doesn't look resolved yet.
